| Category | Details |
|----------|---------|
| **Official name** | 石林 (Shí Lín) – “Stone Forest” |
| **Location** | Shilin Yi Autonomous County, Yunnan Province, China (≈ 70 km north of Kunming) |
| **Coordinates** | 25.0000 ° N, 102.0000 ° E |
| **Best time to visit** | Late spring (April–May) or early autumn (September–October) for mild weather and fewer crowds. |
| **Duration** | 1–2 days (half‑day tour or full day if you want to explore the surrounding villages) |
| **Highlights** | • 1,000+ limestone pillars & stalagmites that look like a forest of stone.<br>• The “Stone Dragon” and “Stone Lion” formations.<br>• The “Stone River” (a natural stone archway).<br>• The “Stone Forest Museum” with geological and cultural exhibits.<br>• Nearby Yi ethnic villages (e.g., Shilin Yi Village) for cultural immersion. |
| **Activities** | • Guided walking tour of the main park.<br>• Photography (especially sunrise/sunset for dramatic lighting).<br>• Cultural performances in the Yi village.<br>• Hiking to the “Stone River” and “Stone Dragon” areas. |
| **Accessibility** | • By train: Kunming to Shilin (≈ 2 h).<br>• By bus: Kunming to Shilin (≈ 2 h).<br>• By car: 70 km from Kunming, 1 h via G214. |
| **Tickets** | • Entrance fee: ~ ¥120 (≈ $18) per adult.<br>• Guided tour packages: ¥250–¥400 (≈ $38–$60) including guide, transport, and lunch. |
| **Nearby attractions** | • **Dali Ancient Town** (≈ 3 h drive).<br>• **Tiger Leaping Gorge** (≈ 4 h drive).<br>• **Kunming Green Lake** (≈ 1 h drive). |
| **Travel tips** | • Wear comfortable walking shoes; the terrain is uneven.<br>• Bring water, sunscreen, and a hat.<br>• The park can get crowded on weekends; consider visiting on a weekday.<br>• Check local weather – the area can be misty in the mornings. |
| **Cultural note** | The Stone Forest is sacred to the Yi people, who consider the stone pillars as “ancient trees” and have legends about spirits living among them. |

